@startuml AI Assistant Participant Diagram
title Figure X: AI Assistant Interaction Participant Diagram

' Professional Sequence Diagram Styling
skinparam actorStyle awesome
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam handwritten false
skinparam monochrome false
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 10
skinparam ParticipantPadding 40
skinparam BoxPadding 10

skinparam sequence {
    ArrowColor #0078d4
    LifeLineBorderColor #0078d4
    LifeLineBackgroundColor #f0f7ff
    
    ParticipantBackgroundColor #f0f7ff
    ParticipantBorderColor #0078d4
    ParticipantFontSize 14
    ParticipantFontColor #0078d4
    
    ActorBackgroundColor #f0f7ff
    ActorBorderColor #0078d4
}

skinparam note {
    BackgroundColor #fff9e6
    BorderColor #d4a017
    FontSize 11
}

actor "Plant Operator" as User
participant "AIChatAssistant.jsx" as UI <<Boundary>>
participant "AssistantService.js" as Service <<Control>>
participant "DashboardContext.js" as Context <<System>>
participant "LLM API" as LLM <<External Service>>
database "LocalStorage" as LS <<Database>>

autonumber

User -> UI : Enter Question & Click "Send"
activate UI

UI -> UI : createUserMessage(content)
UI -> UI : updateThreads(state)

UI -> Service : sendAssistantMessage({question, context, settings, conversation})
activate Service

Service -> Context : getDashboardContext()
activate Context
Context --> Service : Real-time plant data
deactivate Context

Service -> LLM : POST request (question + context + history)
activate LLM
LLM --> Service : JSON {reply, chart, suggestedTitle}
deactivate LLM

Service --> UI : {reply, chart, model}
deactivate Service

UI -> UI : normalizeChartSpec(chart)
UI -> UI : createAssistantMessage(reply)

UI -> LS : saveAssistantThread(updatedThread)
activate LS
LS --> UI : Success
deactivate LS

UI --> User : Display AI Response & Generated Charts
deactivate UI

note right of Service
  **Context Enrichment:**
  The service injects current
  load, efficiency, and wet bulb
  data so the AI "knows" what 
  the plant is doing.
end note

@enduml
